      "sender": "SYSTEM",
      "recipient": "USER",
      "content": "{{USER_INSTRUCTION}}ROUND 1 [provide: image_1, image_2, image_3]\nQuery: I'm updating my inventory list. Check my inventory project to see which of the items in these three photos are already there. The first photo has one item, the second has two, and just look at the main large chip in the third. For any that are missing, create new tasks with their brand and model numbers.\nInstructions: Ask the assistant to check your inventory project for the items shown in the images (the hard drive, the two remotes, and the main large chip on the board) and to create new tasks for any that are not already listed, using their brand and model numbers. Because you have multiple projects with 'inventory' in the name, the assistant should ask you to clarify which one you mean; when it does, specify 'Home Lab Inventory'. If it lists the items it identified and asks if you want to proceed with adding the missing ones, confirm. Once the new tasks are successfully created, move on to the next round.\n\nROUND 2 [provide: image_4, image_5]\nQuery: Here are two more components. Do the same for these - check if they are in the project and add them if they're missing.\nInstructions: Ask the assistant to repeat the exact same process for the two new components shown in these images (the cooling fan and the hard drive). It should check them against the 'Home Lab Inventory' project and add any that are missing as new tasks with their brand and model numbers. If the assistant asks for confirmation before adding the missing item, approve it. When the assistant confirms the final task has been created, end the conversation.\n\nYou have 5 images available to share with the agent using the send_message_with_image tool.\nIMPORTANT: Image IDs are ZERO-INDEXED integers (0, 1, 2, ...). Do NOT add 1 to the IDs.\nAvailable image IDs: [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]\nImage mapping:\n  image_1.jpg -> image ID 0\n  image_2.jpg -> image ID 1\n  image_3.jpg -> image ID 2\n  image_4.jpg -> image ID 3\n  image_5.jpg -> image ID 4\n\n## IMAGE DELIVERY\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f IMPORTANT: You MUST use the `send_message_with_image` tool to share images with User B. Do NOT just describe images in text \u2014 you MUST call the tool.\n\nImage delivery schedule:\n\n  Round 2: YOU MUST call the send_message_with_image tool with image_ids='3,4' \u2014 do NOT write the tool name as text; use the actual function call. Include a natural, conversational message to the assistant."
    },
